</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4. </span>Ablation Studies</h3>

<section id="S5.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.4.1. </span><span id="S5.SS4.SSS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Impact of different DINO variants.</span></h4>

<div id="S5.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Table <a href="#S5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 5.4.1. Impact of different DINO variants. ‣ 5.4. Ablation Studies ‣ 5. Experiments ‣ CoME-VL: Scaling Complementary Multi-Encoder Vision-Language Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we evaluate CoME-VL with different self-supervised backbones by replacing DINOv3 with earlier DINO variants. Results on PixMo show consistent improvements as the self-supervised encoder progresses from DINOv1 to DINOv2 and DINOv3, with CoME-VL achieving the best performance across both understanding and grounding tasks. This highlights the importance of stronger self-supervised spatial representations.</p>
</div>
